solutions.body:
The equations factor as
$$(2x + y)(3x + y - 7) = 0 \quad\text{and}\quad (x + 2y)(x + 3y + 7) = 0.$$
Solve the four linear systems:
- $2x + y = 0,\ x + 2y = 0$: $(0, 0)$;
- $2x + y = 0,\ x + 3y = -7$: $y = -2x$, $-5x = -7$, so $\left(\frac75, -\frac{14}5\right)$;
- $3x + y = 7,\ x + 2y = 0$: $x = -2y$, $-5y = 7$, so $\left(\frac{14}5, -\frac75\right)$;
- $3x + y = 7,\ x + 3y = -7$: adding, $4(x+y) = 0$, so $y = -x$, $2x = 7$: $\left(\frac72, -\frac72\right)$.

**Answer: $(0,0), \left(\frac75, -\frac{14}5\right), \left(\frac{14}5, -\frac75\right), \left(\frac72, -\frac72\right)$**
